      "problem": "Express $\\frac{\\sqrt{x+2}}{\\sqrt{2-x}}\\,$ without radicals in the denominator.",
      "worked_solution": "To remove the radical $\\sqrt{2-x}$ from the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{2-x}$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+2}}{\\sqrt{2-x}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{x+2}}{\\sqrt{2-x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2-x}}{\\sqrt{2-x}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{x+2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2-x}}{(\\sqrt{2-x})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{(x+2)(2-x)}}{2-x} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}-{x}^{2}}}{2-x} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}{2-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
